# heightmap.pdl - the numbers of rmmc_heightmap_op (CONFIG, hand-edited; the op holds none). Desk levels become vox y by  ground_y = H - 1 + shift  (H = the glyph height of map.txt/legend.txt).
# A land column of H levels is solid at y 0..ground_y (kind_top on top, kind_below under it). A WATER tile (a legend SLOT name) is not a solid block: the column has a solid bed
# `depth` blocks under the water surface and the water fills ground_y+1..water_level, where water_level = H - 1 + shift (the top face of the cell). shift must be large enough that no bed is below 0.
RULE  | shift | 3
# WATER | slot name | depth in blocks | bed kind
WATER | water       | 1 | sand
WATER | water_deep  | 2 | sand
